 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Gentle humming helps a lot, like a baby. Rinse with dish soap instead of regular soap on its own, it's too hard on bristles. That's the worst thing. It hydrates them, and the water adds more bacteria. Some can be rescued, if you soak them overnight in warm water. But if they won't soften, better to buy fresh set from the sales. Go for soft brushes on sale, or get a washable roller and paint with a big brush.",
